{"id": "7796ebb5-662d-46e7-bf62-511a14b29abd", "slug": "minimalist-event-launch", "title": "Minimalist Event Launch", "description": "Minimalist Event Heading Component is designed for building reusable UI components in modern web projects. Key features include reusable structure, responsive behavior, and production-ready presentation. It is suitable for component libraries and responsive product interfaces.", "content": "---\nversion: \"neuform-top-creators-featured\"\nname: \"Minimalist Event Launch\"\ndescription: \"Minimalist Event Heading Component is designed for building reusable UI components in modern web projects. Key features include reusable structure, responsive behavior, and production-ready presentation. It is suitable for component libraries and responsive product interfaces.\"\ncolors:\n  primary: \"#F2F2F2\"\n  secondary: \"#FFFFFF\"\n  accent: \"#F2F2F2\"\n  background: \"#F2F2F2\"\n  surface: \"#FFFFFF\"\n  text-primary: \"#111827\"\n  text-secondary: \"#4B5563\"\n  border: \"#E5E7EB\"\ntypography:\n  display-lg:\n    fontFamily: \"Inter\"\n    fontSize: \"64px\"\n    fontWeight: 500\n    lineHeight: \"1.04\"\n    letterSpacing: \"0\"\n  body-md:\n    fontFamily: \"Inter\"\n    fontSize: \"16px\"\n    fontWeight: 400\n    lineHeight: \"1.6\"\n  label-md:\n    fontFamily: \"JetBrains Mono\"\n    fontSize: \"12px\"\n    fontWeight: 600\n    lineHeight: \"1.2\"\nspacing:\n  base: \"8px\"\n  gap: \"16px\"\n  card-padding: \"24px\"\n  section-padding: \"80px\"\nrounded:\n  card: \"8px\"\n  control: \"8px\"\n  pill: \"9999px\"\ncomponents:\n  card:\n    background: \"Use the surface token with subtle borders and HTML-matched shadow depth\"\n    radius: \"Match the declared card radius token\"\n  button:\n    background: \"Use primary or accent colors for the main action\"\n    radius: \"Use the control or pill radius based on the source HTML\"\n---\n# Minimalist Event Launch\nSource: Neuform Featured templates from top creators. Author: Vanh DesignCode (@vanh). Views: 83; favorites: 0; remixes: 0.\nTags: heading, animated, webgl, threejs, dither, effect, branding.\n## Overview\nMinimalist Event Heading Component is designed for building reusable UI components in modern web projects. Key features include reusable structure, responsive behavior, and production-ready presentation. It is suitable for component libraries and responsive product interfaces.\n\nEquinox Dynamics presents Framework 10.24.25 at 8pm PST\n## Composition\nUse the attached HTML reference as the source of truth. Preserve the visible hierarchy, first-screen composition, section rhythm, density, and interaction tone before adapting copy or content.\nKey visible headings include: Equinox Dynamics; Framework.\n## Colors\nAnchor the palette in primary #F2F2F2, secondary #FFFFFF, accent #F2F2F2, background #F2F2F2, surface #FFFFFF, text-primary #111827. Keep background, surface, text, and border roles distinct so generated layouts retain the same contrast pattern as the source.\n## Typography\nUse Inter for display moments and Inter for body copy unless the HTML clearly demands a compatible fallback. Labels and technical metadata should use JetBrains Mono or an equivalent mono face.\n## Layout\nKeep spacing deliberate and stable. Favor the same grid direction, max-width behavior, card density, and responsive stacking seen in the HTML. Do not replace distinctive source structures with generic SaaS sections.\n## Components\nCards, buttons, badges, navigation, and repeated blocks should preserve the source geometry, border treatment, and hover feel.\n## Motion\nPreserve existing motion cues such as masked reveals, staggered entrance, hover lift, scroll-triggered transitions, and ambient movement. Keep easing smooth and restrained.\n## WebGL & Effects\n\nIf the source includes canvas, WebGL, Three.js, gradients, particles, or atmospheric effects, rebuild them as supporting layers behind the content. Keep effects performant, responsive, and secondary to the interface.\n\n## Guardrails\n- Do not flatten the source into a generic card grid.\n- Do not swap the color mode unless the source clearly supports it.\n- Preserve the first viewport signal, focal object, and visual density.\n- Keep buttons, cards, and badges aligned to the same radius and border language.", "preview_html": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\">\n    <title>Minimalist Event Launch</title>\n    <script src=\"https://cdn.tailwindcss.com\"></script>\n    <script src=\"https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/three.js/r128/three.min.js\"></script>\n    <script src=\"https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/gsap/3.12.2/gsap.min.js\"></script>\n    <link href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Inter:wght@100;200;300;400&display=swap\" rel=\"stylesheet\">\n    <style>\n        body {\n            margin: 0;\n            overflow: hidden;\n            background-color: #f2f2f2;\n            font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif;\n            /* Prevent text selection for cleaner app feel */\n            -webkit-user-select: none;\n            -moz-user-select: none;\n            -ms-user-select: none;\n            user-select: none;\n        }\n\n        #webgl-container {\n            position: absolute;\n            top: 0;\n            left: 0;\n            width: 100vw;\n            height: 100vh;\n            z-index: 0;\n        }\n\n        /* Subtle noise texture over everything to bind it together */\n        .noise-overlay {\n            position: absolute;\n            inset: 0;\n            z-index: 5;\n            pointer-events: none;\n            opacity: 0.03;\n            background-image: url(\"data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg viewBox='0 0 200 200' xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'%3E%3Cfilter id='noiseFilter'%3E%3CfeTurbulence type='fractalNoise' baseFrequency='0.65' numOctaves='3' stitchTiles='stitch'/%3E%3C/filter%3E%3Crect width='100%25' height='100%25' filter='url(%23noiseFilter)'/%3E%3C/svg%3E\");\n        }\n    </style>\n</head>\n<body>\n\n    <!-- 3D Background -->\n    <div id=\"webgl-container\"></div>\n    <div class=\"noise-overlay\"></div>\n\n    <!-- UI Overlay -->\n    <div class=\"relative z-10 w-full h-screen flex flex-col justify-between items-center py-12 md:py-16 pointer-events-none\">\n\n        <!-- Top Header -->\n        <header class=\"text-center gs-reveal pointer-events-auto space-y-1\">\n            <h2 class=\"text-xs md:text-sm tracking-[0.3em] text-gray-500 uppercase font-light\">Equinox Dynamics</h2>\n            <p class=\"text-[10px] md:text-xs text-gray-400 font-thin italic tracking-wide\">presents</p>\n        </header>\n\n        <!-- Bottom Footer -->\n        <footer class=\"text-center gs-reveal pointer-events-auto flex flex-col items-center\">\n            <h1 class=\"text-5xl md:text-7xl lg:text-[7rem] tracking-tighter text-gray-800 font-thin uppercase leading-none mb-4 mix-blend-multiply\">\n                Framework\n            </h1>\n            <div class=\"h-px w-12 bg-gray-300 mb-4 opacity-50\"></div>\n            <p class=\"text-xs md:text-sm text-gray-500 font-light tracking-widest lowercase\">\n                10.24.25 at 8pm PST\n            </p>\n        </footer>\n\n    </div>\n\n    <script>\n        // --- Three.js Setup ---\n        const container = document.getElementById('webgl-container');\n        const scene = new THREE.Scene();\n        // Match background color precisely with CSS\n        const bgColor = new THREE.Color(0xf2f2f2);\n        scene.background = bgColor;\n        scene.fog = new THREE.Fog(bgColor, 20, 60);\n\n        const camera = new THREE.PerspectiveCamera(35, window.innerWidth / window.innerHeight, 0.1, 100);\n        // Adjust camera distance based on screen width for responsiveness\n        const camZ = window.innerWidth < 768 ? 45 : 35;\n        camera.position.set(0, -5, camZ);\n        camera.lookAt(0, 0, 0);\n\n        const renderer = new THREE.WebGLRenderer({ antialias: true, alpha: false });\n        renderer.setSize(window.innerWidth, window.innerHeight);\n        renderer.setPixelRatio(Math.min(window.devicePixelRatio, 2));\n\n        // Enable shadows for the embossed look\n        renderer.shadowMap.enabled = true;\n        renderer.shadowMap.type = THREE.PCFSoftShadowMap;\n        container.appendChild(renderer.domElement);\n\n        // --- Lighting ---\n        // Soft ambient light\n        const ambientLight = new THREE.AmbientLight(0xffffff, 0.6);\n        scene.add(ambientLight);\n\n        // Directional light casting shadows (positioned top-left-ish)\n        const dirLight = new THREE.DirectionalLight(0xffffff, 0.8);\n        dirLight.position.set(-10, 20, 15);\n        dirLight.castShadow = true;\n        dirLight.shadow.mapSize.width = 2048;\n        dirLight.shadow.mapSize.height = 2048;\n        dirLight.shadow.camera.near = 0.5;\n        dirLight.shadow.camera.far = 50;\n        dirLight.shadow.camera.left = -20;\n        dirLight.shadow.camera.right = 20;\n        dirLight.shadow.camera.top = 20;\n        dirLight.shadow.camera.bottom = -20;\n        dirLight.shadow.bias = -0.001;\n        scene.add(dirLight);\n\n        // --- Hexagon Generation ---\n        const hexRadius = 1;\n        // Cylinder with 6 radial segments creates a hexagon\n        const geometry = new THREE.CylinderGeometry(hexRadius, hexRadius, 1, 6);\n\n        // Material that catches light softly, color slightly off-white to contrast shadows\n        const material = new THREE.MeshStandardMaterial({\n            color: 0xffffff,\n            roughness: 0.7,\n            metalness: 0.1,\n        });\n\n        const hexagons = [];\n        const gridRadius = 8; // How many rings of hexagons\n\n        // Hexagon grid math\n        const hexWidth = Math.sqrt(3) * hexRadius;\n        const hexHeight = 2 * hexRadius;\n        const xOffset = hexWidth;\n        const yOffset = hexHeight * 0.75;\n\n        // Group to hold all hexes so we can rotate the entire cluster slightly if needed\n        const hexGroup = new THREE.Group();\n        scene.add(hexGroup);\n\n        for (let q = -gridRadius; q <= gridRadius; q++) {\n            let r1 = Math.max(-gridRadius, -q - gridRadius);\n            let r2 = Math.min(gridRadius, -q + gridRadius);\n\n            for (let r = r1; r <= r2; r++) {\n                // Calculate position\n                const x = hexWidth * (q + r/2);\n                const y = yOffset * r;\n\n                // Determine distance from center to shape the cluster\n                const dist = Math.sqrt(x*x + y*y);\n\n                // Create an irregular cluster shape based on distance and some noise\n                // We drop hexagons that are too far, and occasionally drop some closer ones\n                if (dist < 12 && (Math.random() > (dist / 14))) {\n                    const mesh = new THREE.Mesh(geometry, material);\n\n                    // Rotate to point top up\n                    mesh.rotation.x = Math.PI / 2;\n                    mesh.rotation.y = Math.PI / 6;\n\n                    // Initial position (z is depth here because we rotated)\n                    mesh.position.set(x, y, 0);\n\n                    mesh.castShadow = true;\n                    mesh.receiveShadow = true;\n\n                    // Store base data for animation\n                    mesh.userData = {\n                        baseZ: 0,\n                        dist: dist,\n                        randomOffset: Math.random() * Math.PI * 2\n                    };\n\n                    hexGroup.add(mesh);\n                    hexagons.push(mesh);\n                }\n            }\n        }\n\n        // --- Animation Loop ---\n        const clock = new THREE.Clock();\n\n        function animate() {\n            requestAnimationFrame(animate);\n            const time = clock.getElapsedTime();\n\n            // Ambient breathing animation for hexagons\n            hexagons.forEach(mesh => {\n                const data = mesh.userData;\n                // Create a wave effect originating from center + some randomness\n                const wave = Math.sin(time * 1.5 - data.dist * 0.5 + data.randomOffset * 0.2);\n\n                // Morph Z position (which is height towards camera)\n                // Center hexes move more than outer ones\n                const amplitude = Math.max(0, (1 - data.dist / 15)) * 1.5;\n                mesh.position.z = data.baseZ + wave * amplitude;\n            });\n\n            // Very slow rotation of the entire group\n            hexGroup.rotation.z = Math.sin(time * 0.1) * 0.05;\n\n            renderer.render(scene, camera);\n        }\n        animate();\n\n        // --- Responsive Handling ---\n        window.addEventListener('resize', () => {\n            const width = window.innerWidth;\n            const height = window.innerHeight;\n\n            camera.aspect = width / height;\n            // Adjust Z position on mobile\n            camera.position.z = width < 768 ? 45 : 35;\n            camera.updateProjectionMatrix();\n\n            renderer.setSize(width, height);\n        });\n\n        // --- GSAP Animations ---\n        // Subtle reveal for text elements\n        gsap.fromTo('.gs-reveal',\n            {\n                y: 30,\n                opacity: 0\n            },\n            {\n                y: 0,\n                opacity: 1,\n                duration: 2,\n                stagger: 0.3,\n                ease: 'power3.out',\n                delay: 0.5\n            }\n        );\n\n        // Track mouse to slightly shift camera for parallax effect\n        let mouseX = 0;\n        let mouseY = 0;\n        let targetX = 0;\n        let targetY = 0;\n        const windowHalfX = window.innerWidth / 2;\n        const windowHalfY = window.innerHeight / 2;\n\n        document.addEventListener('mousemove', (event) => {\n            mouseX = (event.clientX - windowHalfX) * 0.005;\n            mouseY = (event.clientY - windowHalfY) * 0.005;\n        });\n\n        // Add camera parallax to render loop\n        const originalAnimate = animate;\n        animate = function() {\n            targetX = mouseX * 2;\n            targetY = mouseY * 2;\n\n            camera.position.x += (targetX - camera.position.x) * 0.05;\n            camera.position.y += (-targetY - 5 - camera.position.y) * 0.05; // maintain -5 y offset\n            camera.lookAt(0, 0, 0);\n\n            originalAnimate();\n        };\n\n    </script>\n</body>\n</html>", "preview_file_name": "minimalist-event-launch.html", "thumbnail_url": "https://hoirqrkdgbmvpwutwuwj.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/design-system-thumbnails/regenerated-2026-05-22-2s/minimalist-event-launch.jpg", "source_name": "minimalist-event-launch-DESIGN.md", "views": 267, "forks": 8, "private": false, "featured": true, "created_by": "1a62ed4c-6d0d-4900-8de2-1f3139579949", "created_at": "2026-05-01T16:18:09.070118+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-07-03T21:39:20.988655+00:00"}